course: dictionary
lesson: 2896
title: Doubtful: not sure, or not quite right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Doubtful is an adjective, and it has three main meanings. If you are doubtful about something, you are not sure it is true or will happen. If something is doubtful, it probably will not happen or is probably not true. Doubtful can also describe something that seems not quite honest or good.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A safe rule for doubtful food is: when in doubt, throw it out.» Here doubtful means you cannot be sure the food is safe, so you should not eat it. Swap in "not sure" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The Duchess says she is «doubtful about the temper of your flamingo». She is not sure the flamingo will behave well, so she is a little suspicious. The word shows she is unsure, not that she is certain of anything.
explain: Doubtful often comes with a small helper word, like about, whether or that: «it is doubtful that», «it is doubtful whether». When you see these phrases, the writer is telling you that something is not certain.
fact: Doubtful is an adjective: doubtful, more doubtful, most doubtful.
fact: «Doubtful» means not sure, or probably not true or not going to happen.
fact: «Doubtful» can also describe something that seems not quite honest or good, like a doubtful excuse.
fact: In science, a doubtful result is one you should check again before you believe it.
fact: The noun is doubt, as in «when in doubt, throw it out».
exercise: «A safe rule for doubtful food is: when in doubt, throw it out.» What does doubtful food mean? | Food that is very tasty | Food that is sweet | *Food you cannot be sure is safe to eat | Food that is cooked in a pan
exercise: Grandad says, «It is doubtful whether it will rain today.» What does this mean? | The rain is very loud and heavy right now | It will definitely rain all day | It is raining, and it is a kind of sweet | *Nobody is quite sure it will rain
exercise: Ella says her friend's excuse for being late sounds doubtful. What might doubtful mean here? | It is very long | It is very loud | *It seems not quite honest | It is very funny
test: «Tom gave a doubtful look at the strange, sticky sweets.» What does a doubtful look show? | Tom loves the sweets | Tom is fast asleep | *Tom is not sure about them | Tom is singing a song
test: A scientist says, «Her result is doubtful, so we must test it again.» What should the team do? | *Check the result again | Shout it out to the class | Make the result bigger | Ignore it because it must be correct
exam: «Don't believe everything you read, and only half of what you see» is an old saying about being a little doubtful of exciting stories. What does being doubtful of stories mean? | Believing every story completely | Writing stories as fast as you can | *Not being sure every exciting story is true | Only reading stories about animals
